INSERT INTO hostlist_host_details (host_id,host_experience_years,team_size,motivation,specific_skills,offer_extra_info,business_impact) VALUES (25,8.1,26,'Good mentoring makes room for curiosity, disagreement and a second attempt. I care about leaving behind notes that make the next contribution easier. A useful part of the experience is seeing how a team makes a decision together. The work is scoped so a learner can own a useful slice and explain the trade-offs.','Linux hardening and container scanning; log analysis, detection rules and incident notes; identity policy and least-privilege checks; secure code review and dependency analysis; clear technical notes.','A cross-functional group is maintaining a small incident-response exercise environment. You do not need to arrive as an expert; we agree a realistic scope together. One possible starting point is to turn a threat scenario into a detection rule. The first milestone can lead to a documented experiment with its limitations and next steps. The team offers a weekly check-in and encourages questions in a shared project channel.','["The expected benefit is better evidence for choosing the next product improvement.","A related benefit is more predictable releases with fewer last-minute surprises.","The team is exploring a small incident-response exercise environment, so the result can inform a practical next step."]');
